[stderr] | GAME-011 | GPI-014: cache/update notices and six fixtures | GPI-002–005, 013 | Release + platform | Offline/update/error tests |
[stderr] | GAME-012 | GPI-015: four-target parity/certification matrix | GPI-012–014 | Platform + release | Target evidence and certification checklist |
[stderr] 
[stderr] The machine-readable [inventory](game-production-inventory.json) is
[stderr] authoritative for each original brief, asset/audio linkage, and verification.
[stderr] All referenced visuals (`ASSET-*`) and cues (`AUDIO-*`) are original-production
[stderr] work: each is reviewed for provenance, non-copying, accessibility equivalence,
[stderr] manifest validity, integration trigger, and runtime fallback before release.
[stderr] # 05 — Delivery map
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Inputs:** discovery, game identity/bible, creative/asset/audio direction,
[stderr] technical contract, and [production inventory](game-production-inventory.md).
[stderr] The repository currently contains specifications and Supervisor tooling, not an
[stderr] application source tree. Paths below are deliberate future ownership boundaries,
[stderr] not claims that code already exists. Complete the gated G design collection
[stderr] before F006; never substitute placeholders for `GPI-*` content or creative IDs.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Planned layout and dependency rule
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```text
[stderr] src/core/       deterministic quiz, content, scoring, lifecycle and save rules
[stderr] src/content/    authored QB/TUT sources, schemas, provenance and validators
[stderr] src/platform/   web/PWA and native-wrapper input, storage, cache, audio adapters
[stderr] src/app/        accessible responsive shell, views, settings, feedback
[stderr] assets/         original visual/audio source, manifests and reviewed renders
[stderr] tests/          core, content, platform, app and release evidence
[stderr] docs/           editorial, accessibility, privacy, support and release evidence
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] Each `PW-*` path is reserved exclusively for its row. Target budgets, framework,
[stderr] store accounts, signing, and service vendors remain approval gates; the shared
[stderr] offline client may proceed without inventing them.
[stderr] 
